        "author_association": "NONE",
        "issue_field_values": [],
        "type": null,
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "draft": false,
        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DSpace/DSpace/pulls/2248",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/DSpace/DSpace/pull/2248",
          "diff_url": "https://github.com/DSpace/DSpace/pull/2248.diff",
          "patch_url": "https://github.com/DSpace/DSpace/pull/2248.patch",
          "merged_at": "2021-10-22T15:13:31Z"
        },
        "body": "This PR addresses the following Jira tickets:\r\nhttps://jira.duraspace.org/browse/DS-2718\r\nhttps://jira.duraspace.org/browse/DS-2904\r\nhttps://jira.duraspace.org/browse/DS-4009\r\nFixes #6260\r\nFixes #6078\r\nFixes #7356\r\n\r\nCurrently, DSpace processes Google Analytics events for bitstream synchronously, which can greatly impact both the database connection pool and the ability for users to access bitstreams. Google often is slow to respond to these requests, and has been known to cause serious issues on production systems.\r\n\r\nThis PR addresses these concerns by queueing up events and processing them in a single asynchronous thread. Events are stored in memory in a `CircularFifoBuffer` whose size can be limited (by configuration) if desired. A single thread runs in the background, sleeping, and then checking this list. The thread batches these events into sets of up to 20 (the max supported by the [GA Collection API](https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/protocol/v1/devguide)) and sends a batch request. When the list is empty, the thread sleeps again.\r\n\r\nThe threading was also designed to finish processing these events when DSpace is shutdown. This solution has been tested and proven to work on a production system with heavy traffic.\r\n\r\nI noticed [another PR](https://github.com/DSpace/DSpace/pull/2203) addressing this issue, but was concerned that creating a new thread for every bitstream download event could also result in an exhausted connection pool.",
